  "body": "Slice 1 of #6032 (design #6031). This lands the **pure decision layer** of the generic browser-dependent quota watchdog — the part the issue calls out as the natural fit for PBT/MBT — and leaves the I/O, browser and deployment shell to a follow-up with the boundary written down.\n\n## What lands\n\n`pm-stack/exporters/src/watchdog-state.ts`\n\n- **Failure classes** — `session-expired`, `cookie-missing`, `endpoint-changed`, `browser-down`, `cdp-unreachable`, `rate-limited`, `unknown`, and the single place a class maps to a repair rung.\n- **Repair ladder** — `decide()` returns the next action (`quiet`, `wait-cooldown`, `retry`, `repair rung N`, `human-blocked`, `escalate`) plus the next persisted record. Per-rung attempts are capped at 2 per incident; a rate-limited source sets `cooldownUntil` on disk and the next tick honors it with no browser action; a rate limit whose cooldown rung is spent escalates rather than climbing to a browser repair.\n- **Disk state** — `SourceHealth` carries `lastAttemptAt`, `lastSuccessAt`, `consecutiveFailures`, `currentClass`, sanitized `lastDetail`, `cooldownUntil`, per-rung `rungAttempts`, a bounded (20) `repairLog`, and the incident identity + surfacing flag. `coerceHealth` reads a file back without trusting it: garbage yields a fresh record, never a throw and never an assumed-healthy.\n- **Sanitization** — credential-shaped text is redacted before it can reach the state file or a log.\n\nNo I/O, no browser, no secrets, no provider names — the core is provider-agnostic by construction, which is what the adapter-loader criterion asks for.\n\n## Tests name their oracles\n\n`pm-stack/exporters/test/watchdog-state.test.ts` — **12 pass, 0 fail**:\n\n- **PBT invariants** over generated tick sequences: per-rung attempts never exceed the cap; the repair log stays bounded; `consecutiveFailures` is monotonic while failing and resets on success; a healthy tick always clears the incident and is quiet; no secret-shaped value survives sanitization.\n- **MBT** — a reference model of the ladder written independently of the implementation, stepped in lockstep over 300 generated sequences; any divergence in action, rung, or failure count fails.\n- **Acceptance fixtures**: the broken-source walk (retry → CDP re-validation → re-login → escalation), the rate-limited cooldown persisted and honored then escalating, the human-only challenge marking the incident `human-blocked` with the surfacing flag and not re-hammering, and the healthy source staying quiet.\n\n```bash\ncd pm-stack/aggregator && bun test ../exporters/test/watchdog-state.test.ts\n```\n\nTypecheck of both new files is clean under the repo's strict settings.\n\n## What remains for #6032 (listed in `pm-stack/exporters/README.md`)\n\nThe oneshot entry point (state read/write, `latest.json` + heartbeat reads, history append), the adapter loader and `adapters/`, the rung 2/3 executors, the rung-4 hand-off to #6033, producer scaffolding, and the systemd oneshot + timer. The issue stays open for those.\n\nRefs #6032, #6031.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796757875&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7788&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7788&signature=87840573b93f0a509a6eee3068654fcaadab4fe472ad556ea6d3dd3b0d761a31\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/7788?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->",
